"cardinality-bound"],"id":"small-cardinality-cases","justification":"The empty set sums to 0. A singleton is one of 1 through 8 and hence cannot sum to 9. For a pair {a,b}, write a<b; then a+b=9 and a<9/2, so a=1,2,3,4, producing exactly {1,8}, {2,7}, {3,6}, {4,5}. For a triple a<b<c: if a=1, then b+c=8 and b<c imply b<4, hence b=2 or 3, producing {1,2,6} and {1,3,5}; if a=2, then b+c=7 and 2<b<c imply b<7/2, hence b=3, producing {2,3,4}; if a>=3, then a+b+c>=3+4+5=12. Every displayed set has distinct elements from the ground set and sum 9.","statement":"There are no qualifying subsets of sizes zero or one, exactly four of size two, and exactly three of size three; they are precisely the seven displayed subsets."},{"citations":[],"depends_on":["cardinality-bound","small-cardinality-cases"],"id":"total-count","justification":"Subset cardinalities are disjoint. Sizes 0 and 1 contribute 0, size 2 contributes 4, size 3 contributes 3, and sizes at least 4 are excluded by cardinality-bound. Thus the total is 0+0+4+3=7.","statement":"The exhaustive count is 7."}],"question_status":"answered","tool_requests":[]},"draft_id":"a0006"},"objective":"investigate","output_schema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"challenges":{"items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"attack":{"maxLength":4000,"type":"string"},"claim_id":{"maxLength":64,"pattern":"[a-z][a-z0-9-]{2,63}","type":"string"},"outcome":{"enum":["survives","fails","not_tested"],"type":"string"},"result":{"maxLength":4000,"type":"string"},"tool_ids":{"items":{"maxLength":64,"pattern":"[a-z][a-z0-9-]{2,63}","type":"string"},"maxItems":4,"type":"array"}},"required":["claim_id","attack","result","outcome","tool_ids"],"type":"object"},"maxItems":12,"type":"array"},"checks":{"items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"basis_reasoning":{"maxLength":4000,"type":"string"},"basis_verdict":{"enum":["applicable","not_applicable","unsupported","conditional","source_attributed","not_tested"],"type":"string